order  many consortiums and research groups  have established rich resources of data  collected from normal healthy tissues  and cells  from these healthy samples we can learn  the normal patterns of interaction for  the disease and candidate genes  and use this information to make  predictions  while different types of data should  give us different insights into these  processes some data types appear to  still be underutilized for the task of  disease gene prediction  examples include data types from  resources like encode that provide  insights into the epigenetic regulation  of gene expression  along these lines of improving  performance using prior information you  may have noticed that in valdeo levis's  assessment coexpression data while  helpful did not seem to have a huge  impact on performance relatively  speaking  this is likely because the authors  measured coexpression across 32 tissues  and 45 cell lines  magaret all demonstrated that by  re-weighting a protein protein  interaction network  according to the co-expression of the  specific tissue involved in a disease  they could significantly improve the  performance of their method compared to  when they used a generic protein-protein  interaction network  therefore if the tissues involved in a  disorder are known  then the expression patterns specific to  those tissues could be used to refine  the network  the last few years have seen the  generation of single cell data for many  healthy tissues at various developmental  stages  these data types provide a level of  granularity that may allow for the  determination of different disease gene  networks for specific cell types  another opportunity involves extending  these methods to provide greater insight  into the mechanisms of diseases  while the prediction of disease genes  can advance our understanding of the  disease process by suggesting the  involvement of enriched pathways and  prioritizing genes for further study  there may be additional insig